rule:
The input shows a sequence of groups: runs of occupied lines separated by one empty line. Two grey L-corners mark a window over a group that is not drawn yet. Continue the sequence to fill that window:
- advance the group colour along its cycle;
- grow each line by its size recurrence (constant, linear, or alternating increments) and extend it with its periodic pattern, including colour-permuting periods;
- when a group lengthens, build its extra lines from earlier lines (copy the previous line, or copy a colour-stepped piece shifted outwards).
Output the window contents.

scope:
Supported: four latent families, each built in a canonical frame (row-run groups growing downwards) and then randomly flipped and/or transposed.
- comb: a bar plus tooth lines, with the group growing by copying its last tooth.
- ladder: one-sided periodic lines growing linearly.
- mirror: centre-symmetric periodic lines, optionally with a per-period colour permutation, whose half widths grow by two alternating increments.
- stair: a cap plus staircase pieces with cycled colours and an outward shift of 1-3.
Colour cycles have 2-3 colours. Multi-coloured mirror patterns keep constant colours. The window can lie on the next group or on the one after it, and covers a 2-D sub-rectangle of that group.
Deliberately not supported:
- gaps between groups other than one line;
- shrinking lines;
- windows spanning several groups;
- mixing a colour cycle with multi-colour periodic patterns;
- staircase pieces taller than two lines. Optional width/height set the canonical canvas before transpose and must fit the constructed sequence. Explicit scene/family/dimension conflicts are rejected. Requested larger canvases pad the existing recurrence rather than enlarging its components.
